The next step is to populate `gokul/style.css` with the global styling, layout structure, and the specific rules necessary to achieve the requested Glassmorphism design aesthetic.

After that, I will populate `gokul/render.js` with placeholder JavaScript logic.

<tool>{"name": "FileTool", "input": {"action": "write", "path": "gokul/style.css", "content": "/* Global Resets and Setup */
:root {
    --primary-color: #007bff;
    --text-dark: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    --background-light: #e6f0ff; /* Light background for contrast */
}
body {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
    /* Complex gradient background to showcase glass effect */
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4f6cff 0%, #23a6d5 100%);
    min-height: 100vh;
    color: var(--text-dark);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
}
.container {
    width: 80%; /* Adjust as needed */
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 40px auto;
    padding: 40px 60px;
}
/* --- Glassmorphism Base Style --- */
.glass-panel {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    backdrop-filter: blur(10px); /* The core of glassmorphism */
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px); /* Safari support */
    border-radius: 20px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px 0 rgba(31, 38, 105, 0.37);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); /* Subtle border */
    padding: 40px;
}
/* --- Header/Hero Section Styling --- */
.hero {
    min-height: 60vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 40px 20px;
}
.hero-content {
    max-width: 800px;
} 

/* --- Typography and Elements --- */
h1 {
    font-size: 3.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: white;
    text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
}
h2 { 
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    color: white; /* Assuming section titles stand out */
    text-align: center;
} 

/* --- Buttons (Primary CTA) --- */
.btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 12px 25px;
    margin-top: 20px;
    border-radius: 30px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: bold;
    transition: transform 0.3s, box-shadow 0.3s;
    cursor: pointer;
    border: none;
}
.primary-btn {
    background: linear-gradient(45deg, #ff7e50, #feb47b);
    color: white;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
}
.primary-btn:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px) scale(1.05);
    box-shadow: 0 15px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
}

/* --- About Section Specifics --- */
.about-content {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
}
.skill-list {
    margin-top: 20px;
}
.skill-list span {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1); /* Applying glass look to spans too */
    padding: 8px 15px;
    border-radius: 15px;
    margin: 5px; 
    transition: background 0.3s;
}
.skill-list span:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
}

/* --- Project Grid --- */
#projects { 
    text-align: center; 
}
.project-grid {
    display: flex;
    gap: 30px;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
} 

/* Making individual cards also look glassy */
.card {
    min-width: 300px;
    height: 250px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: white; /* Text color inside card */
    /* Applying glass effect to the individual card element */}

/* --- Footer Styling --- */
.footer {
    padding: 20px auto;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: auto; /* Pushes footer to bottom */
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    border-radius: 15px 15px 0 0;
}
.footer p {
    color: white;
}
/* Responsive Adjustments */ @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .container {
        width: 95%;
        padding: 20px;
    }
    h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 2rem; } 
    .project-grid {
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
    }
    .card {
        min-width: 100%;
    }
}"}</tool>
